mixin () {
  // Static behavioral documentation for the KLIPPER AI PRO backend.
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# KLIPPER AI PRO — Backend API\n\n## Purpose\n\nThe backend turns a YouTube video link into a **clip plan**: it fetches the\nvideo's real transcript, asks an LLM to pick the best moments that fit a chosen\nmaximum clip length, and writes a title, caption and hashtags for each clip.\nPlans are stored per user and can be listed, opened and deleted.\n\nThis backend does **not** download video, cut or join files, burn subtitles, or\nproduce mp4 output. It produces the plan (timestamps + copy) only.\n\n## Public methods\n\n| Method | Kind | Auth | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `generatePlan(request)` | update | signed-in | Fetch transcript, run AI selection, persist a plan. |\n| `listPlans()` | query | signed-in | List the caller's plans, newest first. |\n| `getPlan(id)` | query | signed-in | Read one of the caller's plans by id. |\n| `deletePlan(id)` | update | signed-in | Delete one of the caller's plans. |\n| `schema()` | query | per entity | OQL schema document. |\n| `execute(qJson)` | query | per entity | OQL query endpoint. |\n| `getApiDoc()` | query | anyone | This document. |\n| `transform(input)` | query | anyone | HTTP outcall transform callback (platform use). |\n\n### `generatePlan`\n\nRequest:\n\n```\n{ url : Text; options : { maxClipSeconds : Nat; aspectRatio : AspectRatio; subtitlesEnabled : Bool } }\n```\n\n`aspectRatio` is one of `#portrait` (9:16), `#square` (1:1), `#landscape` (16:9).\n`maxClipSeconds` is the maximum length of each clip in whole seconds\n(30 / 60 / 90 / 180).\n\nResult is a variant:\n\n```\n{ #ok : ClipPlan } | { #err : PlanError }\n```\n\n`PlanError` tags: `#invalidUrl(Text)`, `#noCaptions(Text)`, `#unreachable(Text)`,\n`#aiFailure(Text)`. Each carries a human-readable Indonesian message.\n\n## Authentication and authorization\n\nEvery method except `getApiDoc`, `transform`, and the OQL endpoints requires a\n**signed-in (non-anonymous) caller**. The app's frontend pins an Internet\nIdentity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin`.\nAn agent already holding the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the\ncorrect per-app principal against that origin (for example\n`icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the\nuser's full authority in this app until it expires.\n\nRegistration gates access. A direct API caller must register once by calling\n`_initialize_access_control` as a signed-in caller before any role-guarded\ncall, guarded queries included. The **first** initializer receives the `#admin`\nrole; every subsequent caller receives `#user`. An unregistered caller gets\n`Runtime.trap(\"User is not registered\")` from `getUserRole`, and an anonymous\ncaller is treated as `#guest`. Registration happens only when a caller signs in\nthrough the app's own frontend, so a principal that never did so is\nunregistered even when it belongs to the app's owner, and a signed-in caller\nderived against a different origin is a different principal than the one the\nfrontend registered.\n\nPlan data is **row-scoped per user**: `listPlans`, `getPlan` and `deletePlan`\nreturn or affect only plans whose `owner` equals the calling principal. A plan\nbelonging to another user is invisible and cannot be deleted by a non-owner.\n\n## Units and encoding\n\n- `createdAt` is a **signed nanosecond** timestamp (`Time.now()`), not seconds\n  or milliseconds. Divide by 1_000_000_000 for seconds.\n- `startSeconds` / `endSeconds` / `durationSeconds` / `maxClipSeconds` are whole\n  **seconds**.\n- `hashtags` are plain strings **without** the leading `#`.\n- `id` is a `Nat`; ids are assigned monotonically and never reused.\n- `name` is a display name built from the video title plus the creation\n  timestamp; it is not guaranteed unique across users.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\n`generatePlan` is a single update call that performs two network round-trips\n(transcript fetch, then LLM analysis) and can take several seconds. It returns\nonly when the plan is fully written. There is no server-side job to poll: the\nfrontend should show a pending state for the duration of the call and render the\nreturned plan on success. A `#err` result is terminal for that attempt — the\ncaller may retry with the same or a different link.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\n`generatePlan` is **not idempotent**: each successful call creates a new plan\nwith a new id, even for the same URL. Retrying after a timeout may therefore\nproduce a duplicate plan; the caller should delete the unwanted one.\n`deletePlan` is idempotent — deleting an already-deleted or non-owned id returns\n`false` and changes nothing.\n\n## Errors, limits and gotchas\n\n- Invalid or non-YouTube links return `#invalidUrl`; accepted forms are\n  `watch?v=`, `youtu.be/`, `/shorts/` and `/embed/`.\n- A video with no captions, or an unreachable transcript endpoint, returns\n  `#noCaptions`.\n- An LLM failure or unparseable model output returns `#aiFailure`.\n- The transcript endpoint is bounded to a 1 MB response; very long videos may\n  be truncated by the provider.\n- `generatePlan` requires the platform's inference credentials; if they are\n  absent the call traps rather than returning `#aiFailure`.\n- OQL `clipPlan` rows are scoped per user; the Data Intelligence Agent sees only\n  the calling principal's rows.\n";
  };
};
